<title>NEW ZEALAND: Tranz replaces W&amp;H in NZSE Top 10.</title>
<headline>Tranz replaces W&amp;H in NZSE Top 10.</headline>
<dateline>WELLINGTON 1997-06-09</dateline>
<text>
<p>The New Zealand Stock Exchange said on Monday that Tranz Rail Holdings was to replace publisher Wilson &amp; Horton in the market's Top 10 index following its latest index review. The changes will be effective from July 1.</p>
<p>In the wider-based NZSE40 index, Baycorp Holdings will take the place of Tourism Holdings Limited, and in the NZSE30 index Sanford Limited will be added and Steel and Tube Holdings Limited removed.</p>
<p>While Tranz Rail moves up from the mid-cap index, another share departing that index is Ports of Auckland Limited.  </p>
<p>--Wellington newsroom +64 4 471 4273</p>
